Buttered by critics upon the release of  its first season in 2017 Marvel's Iron  Fist needed some serious image  rehabilitation going into its offer more  outing but the show's reception and  quality actually has started to turn  around and it's even set a Rotten  Tomatoes record in the process according  to the breakdown of data by the review  aggregating site  iein faced a set a record for the  biggest jump in quality between the  first and second seasons of a TV series  at Rotten Tomatoes has ever measured  just because iron fist has clearly  improved doesn't mean this show is  suddenly great now according to the  second season's breakdown on the website  only 50% of critics across 30 reviews  Dinah's series as being worth another  look on an A to F scale that's still a  failing grade though it's definitely a  big improvement over the first season's  19% score when iron fist first season  was released in 2017 critics too righted  the show as being one of the single  worst properties Marvel television had  yet produced it was a feat which to this  date has been exceeded only by ABC's  inhuman series which was released the  same year to a 12 percent Rotten  Tomatoes score despite the major second  season bump from critics it's hard to  characterize iron fist as being a  must-see series yet the finding is  mostly encouraging for viewers who are  already fans of the show with the second  season having a little more of what  people like and a little less of what  they don't  unlike Hannibal or Breaking Bad series  which started good and then got even  better I am first started off terribly  and is now more or less okay even the  more negative reviews for this series  are now characterizing the show as being  fine mildly entertaining or merely  boring  in other words iron fist has stood on  exactly appointment of viewing but it  probably won't ruin your day to see an  episode anymore partially explaining the  turnaround in quality is the fact that  iron fist second season was written  under the guidance of a new showrunner  Raven Metzner  as a screenwriter and producer Metzner  previously worked on the TV series  Sleepy Hollow as well as the show's  heroes reborn falling skies and daybreak  he also wrote the screenplay for the  movie Elektra but that was a long time  ago so we'll try and ignore that Meza  came on board iron fist as a replacement  for season 1 showrunner Scott Burke  who'd earn himself a questionable  reputation as a show run  after overseeing the Showtime serial  killer series texture at the fell from  prestige drama into self-parody  he was also the showrunner for marbles  and humans which was quietly cancelled  after eight profoundly bad episodes  alongside the behind-the-scenes  personnel shifts iron fist second season  also saw marked improvements to a  cinematography and fight choreography  which are generally regarded as being  pretty important ingredients for a  martial arts superhero show the new  season also included an increased focus  on the characters misty Nights and  Colleen Wayne better known in Marvel  Comics as the daughters of the Dragon  season to seize the fighters spend some  time teaming up taking on the bad guys  to enjoyable effect misty also gets a  spiffy new robotic arm while Colleen  earns herself some impressive new powers  in short while iron fist has still the  lowest rated series in the Marvel  Netflix collection it significantly  closed the gap in quality between itself  and the other five shows unfortunately  iron fist second season still seems to  struggle with the same issues that  affect all the shows at Marvel's Netflix  universe whether it's daredevil Jessica  Jones Luke Cage or the Punisher every  one of Marvel's streaming series has  been critiqued to some extent and iron  fist is no exception it still suffers  from problematic pacing some aimless  subplots and occasionally subpar  production values but the season as a  whole is a big step in the right  direction now that 